this will be dealt with in the latter part of our judgment.

</p><p data-structure="Precedent" id="p_119">83.   We may also look at this issue from two other perspectives.

Firstly, the composition of the Appellate Tribunal under <a href="/doc/11697324/" id="a_107">Section 112</a> of

the said Act which mandates that there has to be a Bench of two or

